cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cortex-Bench: enterprise-scale text-to-SQL with domain knowledge, multi-turn sessions and unanswerable questions"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it and state which data snapshot you evaluated against."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Neosapients"
abstract: >-
  Cortex-Bench evaluates text-to-SQL and analytical agents against a single 58-million-row
  synthetic Indian wealth-management database. Its 200 questions span nine tiers, from schema
  linking to multi-turn sessions, and include a tier whose correct answer is that the question
  cannot be answered from the data. Gold answers are compiled by executing reference SQL against
  a frozen snapshot and are valid only against that snapshot.
keywords:
  - text-to-SQL
  - semantic parsing
  - database question answering
  - multi-turn
  - unanswerable questions
  - domain knowledge
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
version: "1.3"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
